                                                "sense_id": "4dec16cd-1e67-35ac-a998-6af14aa812f7",
                                                "text": "\"This means 'that all temporality points beyond itself' (Hart 1973, 32).\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2499b1bc-1a6f-4bd3-83f8-2e1099a26d78",
                                                "sense_id": "4dec16cd-1e67-35ac-a998-6af14aa812f7",
                                                "text": "[1927], 2000 Martin Heidegger Being and Timehttp://books.google.com/books?ie=UTF-8&hl=en&id=9oc2BnZMCZgC&pg=PA302&lpg=PA302&dq=temporality&prev=http://books.google.com/books%3Fq%3Dtemporality&sig=_AHDrBvcln9-ZTvV9JKNgDGazRY\nTemporality makes possible the unity of existence, facticity, and falling prey and thus constitutes primordially the totallity of the structure of care.\nTemporality \"is\" not a being at all. It is not, but rather temporalizes itself. Nevertheless, we still cannot avoid saying that \"temporality 'is' the meaning of care,\" \"temporality 'is' determined thus and so.\""
